Derive PoC signer public keys from their configured private scalars so observer
enrollment cannot drift from the signer processes.

Wire every generated signer companion's durable event observer to its paired
signer and break the companion-health/signer-start dependency cycle. Continuously
verify signer state-machine burn height against its live companion, and surface
persistent drift as a critical authenticated-federation incident.

Synchronize native miner authorization with the companion sortition made
queryable by each burn-block callback. A short callback/RPC ordering window can
no longer leave signers perpetually authorizing the prior tenure or refusing
the newly canonical miner at data-plane admission.

Coalesce signer replay to one bounded provider per reward cycle, rotate after
provider failure, derive current/next-cycle repair pages from the live
signer-event capacity, pause pagination on downstream backpressure, and make
equivocation evidence idempotent. Periodic recovery can no longer multiply the
same replay burst by the signer-set size or hot-loop a refused page.

Stop a rejected old-tenure extension before its next assembly attempt once the
node's canonical Stacks tip shows that the new winner's tenure is active. The
legitimate initial extension window remains unchanged.

Verify libp2p-only operation from each node's live diagnostics instead of a
bounded startup-log tail, and use the canonical exported Prometheus counter
name when checking signer validation observations.

Bound companion validation POSTs by the configured validation deadline, avoid
duplicate synchronous POST retries, and emit `CompanionTimeout` abstention when
the companion stalls. Give monitoring its own short RPC deadline so `/metrics`
continues serving the last snapshot during companion chaos, and bound every
chaos-side RPC probe so cleanup cannot be held indefinitely.

Bound all synchronous signer-runloop companion RPCs by the proposal-validation
horizon. If the canonical sortition view cannot be refreshed for an arriving
proposal, publish `ChainView` unavailability immediately instead of continuing
with cached state and accidentally admitting the proposal after recovery.

Preserve native sync-provider ranking when selecting initial-download status
hedges. Configured bootstrap peers are now preferred as validated recovery
anchors, while an independently rotating secondary provider preserves
failover; pinned peers still obey capability checks, availability backoff, and
invalid-data quarantine.

Classify authenticated sync `Busy` replies as bounded overload rather than
transport unavailability, and jitter retry scheduling by local identity and
request correlation. A simultaneous initial-download fan-in can no longer
exponentially exile a healthy bootstrap or repeatedly elect the same clients
into a small downstream queue.

Add a bounded, per-peer-coalesced FIFO for validated metadata-only sync-control
requests when the shared node handoff is full. Objects, signer replay,
proposals, and arbitrary sync payloads cannot enter this queue;
deferred controls expire to `Busy`, preserving fair multi-page progress and a
strict memory/latency bound.

Serve native sync status from the durable canonical sortition index instead of
the transient per-pass `NetworkResult`. A populated source no longer advertises
height zero between block-processing passes, so simultaneous fresh nodes can
reliably identify and download from the canonical provider.

Bind every paginated inventory/object sync plan to the provider whose status
snapshot established it. Status discovery remains hedged, but a valid empty
inventory from a behind hedge can no longer be spliced into a current source's
plan and falsely complete initial block download.

Track the canonical tip ID as well as its height in the multi-miner Stacks
progress observer. A signer-approved same-height tip replacement now counts as
canonical progress. An unchanged tip is reported as an overlay stall and fails
independent verification while regtest Bitcoin continues producing blocks.

Require every chaos disruption to recover through a fresh canonical Stacks
transition. Bitcoin burn-height progress alone can no longer produce a false
positive recovery result.

Preserve all independently correlated status hedges when a behind peer replies
first in both initial download and steady state, avoiding avoidable sync delay.

Replace the zero-delay compact-epoch cadence with fixed five- and twenty-second
intervals, leaving room for one bounded ten-signer validation retry, and deploy
the historical sBTC interface fixtures at Epoch 3 activation so reward-cycle
anchors and contracts settle before Epoch 4.

Add bounded flash- and slow-Bitcoin cadence events to the chaos runner. A
cadence event succeeds only after a later Bitcoin block and canonical Stacks
transition, so timing variance cannot be mistaken for network recovery.

Apply seeded, replayable Bitcoin timing entropy after Epoch 4: most intervals
remain near 20 seconds, with bounded flash and one-minute tails. Explicit chaos
signals remain available for deterministic cadence scenarios.

Install a detached bounded unpause failsafe around verifier convergence pauses,
so external termination of the controlling shell cannot strand the Bitcoin
cadence container while leaving the PoC apparently stopped.

Treat source-bound miner proposals for a not-yet-observed sortition as bounded
canonical-view-pending work instead of invalid GossipSub traffic. They now
produce an immediate local abstention observation without binding, relaying,
object fetch, journal admission, signer-attributable wire disclosure, or a
false rejection, and are released only after the companion-derived snapshot
confirms the tuple. A clean 28-actor preflight exposed three such background
participation losses per signer in roughly 20 minutes, correlated across the
whole signer set; a companion pause extended the affected signer to thirteen.
Availability-only handoff is itself retried under signer-event backpressure, so
a full bounded queue cannot silently discard the abstention before later
canonical release.

Serve signer Prometheus snapshots independently from synchronous companion
collection. A bounded background refresher retains the last good companion
gauges while `/metrics` continues exposing live process counters throughout a
companion outage. Companion chaos now retries bounded metric probes and requests
periodic flash sortitions until a real unavailable proposal is observed.

Recover chaos targets by resolved container ID instead of `docker compose
start`, preventing Compose from restarting or gating on unrelated dependency
containers outside the selected failure domain.

Drain authenticated native signer events through one process-lifetime miner
router instead of only while an elected miner is waiting for a proposal. A
generation-safe bounded handoff attaches the current coordinator accumulator;
non-winning miners no longer fill the service queue and repeatedly re-observe
uncommitted GossipSub envelopes between tenures. Router saturation remains
visible through the existing event-queue diagnostic.
